  "notes": [
    {
      "topic": "admission",
      "text": "Qualified freshman and transfer students who indicated interest in the major on their applications are accepted directly into the major upon admission to the University. Students who did not apply, or were not accepted, may apply provided their cumulative GPA (including transfer coursework from other institutions) is 3.2 or higher. Applications go to the College of Business Office of Student Services."
    },
    {
      "topic": "grading",
      "text": "Many Business courses must be taken for a letter grade and do not offer a G/P/NC option. See the courses without G/P/NC option list."
    },
    {
      "topic": "other",
      "text": "BUS 475, BUS 476 (Undergraduate Teaching Practicum I, II) and BUS 487 (Independent Research) count toward the total University credit requirement but not toward the business major."
    },
    {
      "topic": "other",
      "text": "The Business Honors Program (BHP) is optional and not evaluated here. It requires BUS 380, BUS 495, and BUS 496, a cumulative GPA of 3.5 or higher, and an application."
    },
    {
      "topic": "other",
      "text": "The page's C-minimum grade rule lists BUS courses, ECO 110, ECO 111, and MAT 122. ACC courses are not named in that rule, so the minimum-grade policy on the specialization requirement may apply more broadly than the page states; confirm with the program office."
    }
  ],
